cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Blackwell's trapdoor channel: certified capacity bounds 0.5749319 <= C <= 0.5749683"
authors:
  - name: "Moki & Julio"
version: "1.0"
license: CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - trapdoor channel
  - channel capacity
  - certified computation
  - duality upper bound
  - finite-state channels
  - ball arithmetic
abstract: >-
  Blackwell's trapdoor channel (1961) has no known capacity. This release certifies
  0.57493196741521 <= C <= 0.574968285761 bits per drop, an interval of width 3.632e-5. The floor
  is the certified information rate of an explicit run-length input recipe (1,920 hidden states, depth 24, with a
  written rounding-error bound). The ceiling is an order-15 output model checked by the duality method in exact
  integer arithmetic with upward-rounded ball logarithms. The ceiling was re-checked by a second verifier written
  from the definitions, and the floor by an independent exact evaluator at depths 11 and 12. Sealed
  (pre-registered) tests, proofs, referee reports, certificates and transcripts are included. Code is
  MIT-licensed (LICENSE-CODE). Written with AI assistance.
